<p>Las Palmas is a genuine Spanish city rather than a resort zone, spread across neighbourhoods that each have their own character: the historic Vegueta quarter, the long Las Canteras beach promenade, the commercial strip around Mesa y López, and the Puerto de la Luz port and cruise terminal. A private driver takes that layout into account, delivering you to your specific address rather than a single generic drop-off point, which matters more here than it would within Puerto Rico's compact resort footprint. For more background on the capital, see our <a href="/las-palmas-de-gran-canaria/">Las Palmas de Gran Canaria</a> guide.</p>
